From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:52:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 331/342] freebsd_wlan: no routine debug output, it makes USB
 audio skip

Kernel debug output is written to the serial port with interrupts off on
the printing CPU, milliseconds a line, whether anything is attached or not.
On a C2 on Wi-Fi the Wi-Fi layer printed a line for every wireless ioctl
(TRACE_WLAN: 162 in 40 minutes) and four lines each time the access
point's beacon changed its WME parameters, among other routine net80211
messages; dwc2's timer that arms USB audio packets came up to 8.4 ms late
and a packet was skipped about every two minutes, the stutters left after
+334. On the test board, kernel output from a driver during playback gave
5 skipped packets, 30 split gaps and a timer 16.5 ms late in 2 minutes,
and with serial_debug_output off none, the timer within 104 us.

TRACE_WLAN is off, and a vap's net80211 debug messages are only those of
the connection's state: association, authentication, state changes,
802.11h and roaming (no more WME, node, rate and inactivity messages).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../freebsd_wlan/net80211/ieee80211_haiku.cpp      | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_wlan/net80211/ieee80211_haiku.cpp b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_wlan/net80211/ieee80211_haiku.cpp
index 5989443667..be09531c4f 100644
--- a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_wlan/net80211/ieee80211_haiku.cpp
+++ b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_wlan/net80211/ieee80211_haiku.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,10 @@ extern "C" {
 #include <shared.h>
 
 
-#define TRACE_WLAN
+// Every line of kernel debug output goes to the serial port with interrupts
+// off on its CPU, milliseconds each: these traces, and the routine net80211
+// messages below, made a board's USB audio skip packets (PLAN.md M82).
+//#define TRACE_WLAN
 #ifdef TRACE_WLAN
 #	define TRACE(x...) dprintf(x);
 #else
@@ -809,14 +812,13 @@ ieee80211_vap_xmitpkt(struct ieee80211vap *vap, struct mbuf *m)
 void
 ieee80211_sysctl_vattach(struct ieee80211vap* vap)
 {
-	vap->iv_debug = IEEE80211_MSG_XRATE
-		| IEEE80211_MSG_NODE
-		| IEEE80211_MSG_ASSOC
+	// only what the connection does, not what it carries: the WME
+	// parameters came again with every change in the access point's beacon
+	// (four lines a time), the nodes and rates with every reference
+	vap->iv_debug = IEEE80211_MSG_ASSOC
 		| IEEE80211_MSG_AUTH
 		| IEEE80211_MSG_STATE
-		| IEEE80211_MSG_WME
 		| IEEE80211_MSG_DOTH
-		| IEEE80211_MSG_INACT
 		| IEEE80211_MSG_ROAM;
 }
 
